Subject: [PATCH] SwiftPM: use CMake's Swift compilation mode abstraction

CMake 3.29 introduced CMP0157 and split Swift compilation from linking when
using the Ninja generator. SwiftPM still selects the old policy through its
3.24 minimum, so CMake 4.x emits a combined incremental compile-and-link
command for the bootstrap executable.

When Ninja needs to relink that executable without recompiling its unchanged
Swift source, the Swift driver attempts to resolve a synthesized temporary
module output and fails:

    error: cannotResolveTempPath(main-1.swiftmodule)

Select the modern policy when the installed CMake supports it. This retains
incremental compilation while giving Ninja distinct object compilation and
link actions. Older supported CMake releases keep the existing behavior.

Sentinel: NUCLEUS_SWIFTPM_CMAKE_SWIFT_COMPILATION_MODE

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 2e5fe668..2da59664 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -12,6 +12,10 @@ endif()
 
 cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.24)
 
+if(POLICY CMP0157)
+  cmake_policy(SET CMP0157 NEW)
+endif()
+
 list(APPEND CMAKE_MODULE_PATH ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/cmake/modules)
 
 project(SwiftPM LANGUAGES C Swift)

diff --git a/Sources/swift-bootstrap/CMakeLists.txt b/Sources/swift-bootstrap/CMakeLists.txt
index cd3a13bb..6d98f75d 100644
--- a/Sources/swift-bootstrap/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Sources/swift-bootstrap/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@
 
 add_executable(swift-bootstrap
     main.swift)
+set_target_properties(swift-bootstrap PROPERTIES
+  Swift_MODULE_NAME swift_bootstrap)
 target_link_libraries(swift-bootstrap PRIVATE
   ArgumentParser
   Basics
